{% comment %}
  EPIR Customer Privacy bridge for the Online Store cookie banner.

  layout/theme.liquid renders the vendor snippet `cookie-banner` (not stored in
  this repo). That banner does not call customerPrivacy.setTrackingConsent, so
  Shopify never sets analyticsProcessingAllowed and the app web pixel stays unloaded.

  This asset listens only inside that banner:
    Zaakceptuj → setTrackingConsent({ analytics, marketing, preferences, sale_of_data } all true)
    Odrzuć     → the same object, all false
  Same object as packages/ui CustomerPrivacyConsentBridge. No call on page load.
  Does not send pixel events and does not treat the pixel as strictly necessary.

  Theme push (after operator approval), these files only:
    layout/theme.liquid
    snippets/epir-customer-privacy-consent.liquid
    assets/epir-customer-privacy-consent.js
{% endcomment %}
<script src="{{ 'epir-customer-privacy-consent.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
